{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-163716",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,\\sqrt{3-{x}^{2}}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{9-3{x}^{2}}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14130823/assets/8ac2ade388bcc0dee28b1a5bbaf0807ae253c0c785b9a63978014e873fe8a1ce.png)\n\nAlso, the distance between a point and the line $x=1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-1|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k|y|=ky,$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3-{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{9-3{x}^{2}}}ky\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{\\sqrt{3-{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{9-3{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(9-3{x}^{2}-(3-{x}^{2}))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(6-2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(3-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k\\cdot {[3x-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{16k}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=ky=\\frac{3}{16}My.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3-{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{9-3{x}^{2}}}\\frac{3}{16}My|x-1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3-{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{9-3{x}^{2}}}\\frac{3}{16}My(x-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}M{\\int }_{-1}^{1}y(x-1)^{2}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3-{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{9-3{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}M{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x-1)^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{\\sqrt{3-{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{9-3{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}M{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x-1)^{2}(3-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}M{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(-{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-6x+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}M{[-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}+\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}-3{x}^{2}+3x]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}M(-\\frac{2}{5}+0+\\frac{4}{3}-0+6) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}M\\cdot \\frac{104}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{13M}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
